From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: sun4i-usb: a role switch's port a peripheral until it decides

With `usb-role-switch` (0042), the role is -1 until the switch is first
set, and meanwhile id and VBUS follow dr_mode, which EHCI0/OHCI0 set to
host as they probe. With the PinePhone on a dock at boot, EHCI0 took the
port and enumerated the dock's hub, then the ANX7688 set the device role
(the dock powers the phone, so it is first the host by Type-C rules) and,
after the data role swap two seconds later, host again: EHCI0 then timed
out reading the hub's descriptor, for good. A replug, starting from the
device role, enumerates. The port is now a peripheral from the start
with a role switch, as it is without one (the gadget, also should the
Type-C controller's driver not probe). A full-speed device behind the
dock's hub (a 2.4 GHz mouse receiver) may still time out at first and
enumerate once replugged.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -799,6 +799,16 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	data->usb_role = -1;
+	/*
+	 * Its role decided by a Type-C controller (`usb-role-switch`, the
+	 * PinePhone's ANX7688): a peripheral until it says otherwise, as
+	 * without one. Not following the host controllers' dr_mode then: probed
+	 * with a dock attached, EHCI0 took the port and enumerated its hub, the
+	 * controller's first role was the device (the dock powers the phone),
+	 * and given back after the data role swap EHCI0 timed out on the hub.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "usb-role-switch"))
+		data->usb_role = USB_ROLE_DEVICE;
 
 	data->base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(pdev, "phy_ctrl");
 	if (IS_ERR(data->base))
